.Dd November 10, 2026
.Dt SCHEME_REGISTER 2
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm scheme_register
.Nd register a scheme server handle under a name
.Sh SYNOPSIS
See the
.Pa raven-abi
crate (syscall number 0x60).
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The .Nm system call is part of the scheme IPC protocol (see
.Xr scheme 7
and
.Pa architecture/03-system-servers.md ).
It registers a scheme name for the calling process after the
.Dv ADMIN
self-handle check; the name must match the scheme-name grammar.
.Pp
Ticket S16 implements namespace prefix mutations and enforces them in
.Xr open 2 ;
registration enforcement is staged so that the current services, whose names are snapshotted
before spawn, keep working.  Until the follow-up flips the check, any valid name may be
registered; the namespace rules will then apply to registration as well.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr open 2 ,
.Xr proc_namespace 2
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD ABI v1.
